language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Find a minimum-length Golomb ruler: size marks 0 = a_1 < ... < a_size whose pairwise differences are all distinct.
given size : int(2..)
find marks : matrix indexed by [int(1..size)] of int(0..size*size)
find length : int(0..size*size)

minimising length
such that
$ the first mark is at position 0 (the ruler starts at 0)
marks[1] = 0,
$ the marks are strictly increasing, so the ruler is ordered from left to right
forAll i : int(1..size-1) . marks[i] < marks[i+1],
$ the length of the ruler is the position of its last mark
length = marks[size],
$ all differences a_j - a_i for i < j are distinct
allDiff([marks[j] - marks[i] | i : int(1..size), j : int(1..size), i < j])
